<br>
On Saturday, August 11th, we headed over to Kael to take down Derakor the Vindicator and the Statue.  Dasani contacted one of our officers, and expressed his interest in attending the raid.  Our officer said it was fine for him to attend, and so he headed over.<br>
<br>
We engage Derakor the Vindicator (Henceforth, referred to as Vindi), and kill him.  As usual, he drops a head (which is no drop) and another item, which was a set of boots in this case.  The head is part of a quest for druids to obtain Gloves of Earthcrafting.  While our officers are discussing which members should receive the drops, we had another member &quot;holding&quot; the body.<br>
<br>
We make a decision on the boots, and announce it in guildchat.  At this point the member holding the body gets up so the person awarded the boots, can loot the boots.  Between the time that the person holding the body gets up, and the time that the awarded person goes to loot the body, Dasani clicks on the body and ninjaloots the Head.  When the person awarded the boots can finally get on the body, he only sees a pair of boots and loots them, as he should have.  At this point, we don't know who ninjalooted the head, and frankly thought that perhaps it was an accident.  We have everyone check their inventory in case it was an accident, and start asking our invites if they looted it.  Dasani was asked specifically in tells by one of our officers if he looted the Head from Vindi.  Dasani responded by saying he did not.<br>
<br>
At this point, after no one has stepped forward and admitted to accidentally or mistakenly looting the head, about 15-20 minutes have passed.  I was rather in incensed at the time, since it was apparent, someone ninjalooted the head.  The next step we take is to petition a GM, and ask for assistance in the Ninjalooting.<br>
<br>
We proceed to engage and kill the Statue.  Our raid and goals done for the day, we head on over to ToV.  While in transit to ToV, a GM contacts us about our petition.  We tell the GM what transpired, the GM said that they would look into the matter.  After about 10 minutes of discussion and clarification, the GM finds out who the culprit is.  About 5 minutes after this, Trinitii (who we awarded the quest item to, and told the GM as such) is approached by Dasani.  Dasani then hands Trinitii the quest item in a trade window  (remember, this is a no drop item, so we believe the GM was actually the one who was doing it, or was somehow involved).<br>
<br>
Shortly after this, the guild that Dasani was in, removes him from their ranks.  The next day, I'm being told by CIW members that Dasani has been trying to provoke them into responding to him.  The day after that he makes a post on CIW's message board claiming that we were harassing him, without any names, evidence or proof.  He was asked to stop flaming on our board, but he proceeded to anyway, and we have removed his posting rights.<br>
<br>
Just wanted to give everyone a heads up about this person, and what you might be able to expect from him, behavior wise.<br>
<br>
I can be contacted at:  aosinator@eqraid.org <p><center>
